      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "That darkness you're describing is incredibly heavy, but it doesn't have to be permanent. When the fuel runs out, it often means the engine needs to be taken apart and examined, not just pushed harder. Think of this emptiness not as a final destination, but as a profound exhaustion that begs for a period of rest and re-evaluation. Perhaps the answer isn't to *keep* going, but to stop and simply *be* for a while.",
      "source": "target",
